
==============================================================================
0. DATA SANITY -- quantisation (FINDINGS 1.1: bare IF sits on 4-7 ADC codes)
==============================================================================
  fan cfgB     (200, 128, 100)     61 distinct codes, span  60.0 LSB  (that span IS the ramp)
  fan cfgA     (240, 2000)         50 distinct codes, span  50.0 LSB  (that span IS the ramp)
  person cfgA  (240, 2000)         49 distinct codes, span  48.0 LSB  (that span IS the ramp)
  empty cfgA   (160, 2000)         51 distinct codes, span  50.0 LSB  (that span IS the ramp)
  -> the target signal is far below one LSB; only FFT processing gain exposes it.

==============================================================================
1. GEOMETRY -- what each config can physically resolve
==============================================================================
  Config A: fs=100000 spc=2000 ramp=50 Hz -> PRF 50 Hz, chirp 20 ms
            S=9.000e+09 Hz/s, range bin 0.833 m, v_unambiguous +-0.155 m/s
            range-Doppler coupling 2.68 m per m/s -> a 10 m/s blade tip lands
            27 m away from 2.5 m.
            *** Config A CANNOT hold fast blade energy in the 2.5 m bin. It is a
                valid test for the SLOW parts of the fan only. ***
  Config B: PRF 1000 Hz, chirp 1 ms, v_unambiguous +-3.11 m/s, coupling 0.134 m
            per m/s -> a 10 m/s blade smears only 1.3 m. Right config for a fan.

