==============================================================================
5. The 51 Hz feature at 0.83 m: a target, or modulation of the feedthrough?
==============================================================================
  A target return scales with RANGE. A modulation of the transmitter feedthrough
  scales with the FEEDTHROUGH. Those predictions differ, so the data can decide:

 range m  feedthru dB  51Hz sb dB  noise dB  sb-noise  sb/feedthru
    0.00       -21.41      -53.79    -58.12      4.33       -32.38
    0.83       -13.76      -45.55    -48.25      2.70       -31.79
    1.67       -15.17      -42.53    -43.29      0.76       -27.37
    2.50       -33.63      -43.06    -42.99     -0.07        -9.43
    3.33       -33.35      -43.23    -43.27      0.04        -9.88
    4.16       -29.00      -43.67    -43.46     -0.20       -14.66
    5.00       -35.72      -43.97    -43.65     -0.32        -8.25

  sb/feedthrough is ~constant wherever the feedthrough is large, and the moment
  the feedthrough falls 20 dB (at >=2.5 m) the sideband falls to EXACTLY the noise
  floor. It tracks the feedthrough, not range.
  >>> The 51 Hz sidebands are amplitude modulation of the TX feedthrough (vibration
      or an electrical artefact), NOT a range-resolved return from the fan. With no
      fan-OFF Config B capture in existence, whether the fan CAUSES them is untested.

  sideband centroid = 51.83 Hz (a 3-blade fan at 1037 rpm -- entirely plausible),
  so it is worth asking the CW data whether a coherent 52 Hz line exists at all.

  RESOLUTION-SCALING TEST. A coherent narrow line gains ~3 dB of contrast for every
  halving of the FFT bin width, because its power stays in one bin while the noise
  floor per bin drops. Broadband noise gains nothing. 60 Hz mains is the control.

  bin Hz      fanA      fanB     empty   fan-empty |  60Hz (ctrl)
   2.000     -0.07      0.00     -0.84        0.81 |        13.28
   1.000      0.49      0.28     -0.43        0.81 |        16.10
   0.500      1.21      0.63      0.61        0.31 |        19.09
   0.250      1.68      1.67      1.85       -0.18 |        21.84
   0.125      2.17      2.98      2.81       -0.24 |        23.96

  the 60 Hz control climbs 13.3 -> 24.0 dB (+2.7 dB per halving) exactly as a
  coherent line must. The 51.8 Hz fan-minus-empty excess stays flat near 0.8 dB and
  then goes NEGATIVE. There is no coherent 51.8 Hz line in the CW data.
  >>> the Config B sideband is an FMCW-mode feedthrough artefact, uncorroborated by
      CW, and NOT evidence of a fan.

