6. SENSITIVITY BY INJECTION -- what return WOULD Config B have found?
==============================================================================
  inject a point scatterer at 2.5 m (f_beat 3002 Hz), v=1.5 m/s (f_d 241 Hz,
  mains-clean), random phase per CPI, into the REAL fan-on data.

   amp uV rms     / LSB        z
         0.00    0.0000     2.31
         0.71    0.0021     2.82
         1.41    0.0042     3.89
         2.12    0.0063     4.85
         3.54    0.0105     8.77
         7.07    0.0210    22.05
        14.14    0.0421    40.05
        35.36    0.1052   102.69

  >>> Config B would have detected a 1.44 uV rms IF return at 2.5 m
      = 0.0043 LSB = -47.3 dB BELOW one ADC code (that is the FFT processing gain).
      The real fan produced nothing above the 3.93 sigma bar, so the fan's IF
      return is below 1.44 uV rms.

==============================================================================
7. CW CROSS-CHECK (independent of FMCW; gain-invariant line contrast)
==============================================================================
  Absolute levels are NOT comparable: the fan-on 50 kSa/s runs sit ~3 dB BELOW the
  day-earlier empty baseline (118/108 uV rms vs 158 uV), so an absolute difference
  measures session gain, not the fan. Compare each spectrum's LINE CONTRAST against
  its own running median instead -- gain-invariant, and a blade line is a narrowband
  peak, which survives any broadband offset. Averaging is equalised in both pairs.

  50 kSa/s, 60 s each (equal averaging)  (60 s each)
    max fan-on excess +1.62 dB at 51.0 Hz (0.317 m/s), sigma_measured 0.52 dB
    -> 3.1 sigma; 1897 non-mains bins searched, chance bar 3.89 sigma -> NO DETECTION

  100 kSa/s, both truncated to 6 s (equal averaging)  (6 s each)
    max fan-on excess +5.33 dB at 1332.0 Hz (8.276 m/s), sigma_measured 1.60 dB
    -> 3.3 sigma; 1897 non-mains bins searched, chance bar 3.89 sigma -> NO DETECTION

